     xmlns:worksheet="http://uow.edu.au/isit906/thestar/digitalcare:worksheet#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://uow.edu.au/isit906/thestar/digitalcare">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="http://uow.edu.au/isit906/thestar/digitalcare/version8"/>
        <worksheet:competencyQuestion>1. Competency Questions!A10:I10 | A=CQ6 | B=Which Alzheimer’s symptoms written for older people were published most recently I can read in larger text size? | C=Chen —Older adult | D=FR02, CR02, CR03, TR03 | E=Multi-relationship | F=OlderAdult —hasCondition→ HealthCondition —hasSymptom→ Symptom ←describes— Guide —isRelatedTo→ DementiaType | G=4 | H=Yes | I=[BLANK]</worksheet:competencyQuestion>
        <worksheet:competencyQuestion>1. Competency Questions!A11:I11 | A=CQ7 | B=Which Alzheimer’s guides are written for older people and available in Chinese? | C=Chen —Older adult | D=FR02, CR03, CR04 | E=Multi-relationship | F=OlderAdult ←isIntendedFor— Guide —isRelatedTo→ AlzheimersDementia and Guide —isAvailableIn→ Language (Chinese) | G=3 | H=Yes | I=[BLANK]</worksheet:competencyQuestion>
        <worksheet:competencyQuestion>1. Competency Questions!A12:I12 | A=CQ8 | B=Is there a care centre near my area in Victoria with someone who speaks Chinese? | C=Chen —Older adult | D=CR05, FR01, FR03 | E=Multi-relationship | F=OlderAdult —isLocatedIn→ Location (Victoria) ←isLocatedIn— CareCentre —hasStaffMember→ StaffMember —speaksLanguage→ Language (Chinese) | G=4 | H=No | I=Add suburb/postcode or coordinates and a distance measure so care centres can be ranked by proximity to the older adult.</worksheet:competencyQuestion>
        <worksheet:competencyQuestion>1. Competency Questions!A13:I13 | A=CQ9 | B=Is there a guide that can help me compare different dementia symptoms my mother might experience? | C=Sarah—Unpaid carer | D=FR02, CR01, CR03 | E=Multi-relationship, Counting | F=Guide —isRelatedTo→ Symptom (×2, e.g. MemoryLoss and Confusion); Symptom is a subclass of InformationTopic | G=2 | H=Yes | I=[BLANK]</worksheet:competencyQuestion>
        <worksheet:competencyQuestion>1. Competency Questions!A5:I5 | A=CQ1 | B=Mum’s dementia is getting harder to manage, and I don’t know where to start. Where I can find a simple guide written for carers how to deal with difficult daily tasks struggling of my mother? | C=Sarah—Unpaid carer | D=FR01, FR02, CR01, CR03 | E=Multi-relationship | F=Carer —caresFor→ OlderAdult —hasCondition→ HealthCondition ←addresses— Guide —isRelatedTo→ DailyTaskStruggling | G=4 | H=Yes | I=[BLANK]</worksheet:competencyQuestion>
        <worksheet:competencyQuestion>1. Competency Questions!A6:I6 | A=CQ2 | B=Which dementia guides for carers about my mum’s type of dementia have been reviewed by a healthcare professional? | C=Sarah—Unpaid carer | D=FR02, CR03, GR04 | E=Multi-relationship | F=Carer —caresFor→ OlderAdult —hasCondition→ HealthCondition ←addresses— Guide —isReviewedBy→ HealthcareProfessional; Guide —isRelatedTo→ DementiaType
 | G=5 | H=Yes | I=[BLANK]</worksheet:competencyQuestion>
        <worksheet:competencyQuestion>1. Competency Questions!A7:I7 | A=CQ3 | B=How many reliable and nearest support services or organisations in NSW I can call for help in case of mother&apos;s urgencies? | C=Sarah—Unpaid carer | D=CR05, FR01, FR03 | E=Multi-relationship, Counting | F=Carer —caresFor→ OlderAdult —hasCondition→ HealthCondition ←supportsCondition— SupportService —isLocatedIn→ Location | G=4 | H=No | I=Add reliability status, phone number and postcode/distance data so services can be filtered, counted and ranked by proximity.</worksheet:competencyQuestion>
        <worksheet:competencyQuestion>1. Competency Questions!A8:I8 | A=CQ4 | B=Which dementia care guides for carers can I download or print to read offline on smartphone? | C=Sarah—Unpaid carer | D=FR02, FR04, CR03, TR01 | E=Multi-relationship | F=Carer ←isIntendedFor—  Guide —isAvailableInFormat→ DocumentFormat
isDownloadable: true / isPrintable: true | G=2 | H=Yes | I=[BLANK]</worksheet:competencyQuestion>
        <worksheet:competencyQuestion>1. Competency Questions!A9:I9 | A=CQ5 | B=Can I search for Alzheimer’s symptoms without giving the website my privacy information? | C=Chen —Older adult | D=FR01, GR01, GR02 | E=Multi-relationship | F=HealthCondition —hasSymptom→ Symptom ←describes— Guide —isGovernedBy→ PrivacyPolicy | G=3 | H=No | I=Add a boolean attribute such as requiresPersonalInformationForSearch = false to represent anonymous symptom searching.</worksheet:competencyQuestion>
        <worksheet:logicalReconciliation>Sample predicate isRelatedto is asserted with the declared property isRelatedTo; the original case is retained verbatim in ws:sampleRow and the mapping CSV.</worksheet:logicalReconciliation>
        <worksheet:sourceSHA256>FAA1D4EF530B952BB592E2B8FC785964ADB1EDBACD640019FC3E4B8B1BA95C8A</worksheet:sourceSHA256>
        <worksheet:sourceWorkbook>ISIT906_TheStar_DigitalCare_Model_Worksheet_v2.xlsx</worksheet:sourceWorkbook>
        <worksheet:teamName>The Star</worksheet:teamName>
        <worksheet:temporaryIRIReason>Read me first!C68 ontology IRI is blank; D68 is only an ISIT406/team07 example and was not used.</worksheet:temporaryIRIReason>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A11:D11 | A=HealthCondition | B=Class | C=Hierarchical Health Condition taxonomy with topic pages, applied to Guides, Symptoms and Support Services. | D=CQ1, CQ2, CQ3, CQ5, CQ6, CQ7</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A12:D12 | A=DementiaType | B=Class | C=Child terms/pages within the Health Condition taxonomy, used to filter condition-specific Guides and Symptoms. | D=CQ2, CQ6, CQ7</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A13:D13 | A=AlzheimersDisease | B=Class | C=Dedicated Alzheimer&apos;s topic page and taxonomy term under DementiaType. | D=CQ7</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A14:D14 | A=Symptom | B=Class | C=Symptom Custom Post Type with searchable pages and links to related conditions and Guides. | D=CQ5, CQ6</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A15:D15 | A=DailyTaskStruggling | B=Class | C=Child category/term within the Symptom structure, used to group practical daily-task Guides. | D=CQ1</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A16:D16 | A=Guide | B=Class | C=Guide Custom Post Type with fields for title, publication/review dates, reading level, download/print links and accessibility information. | D=CQ1, CQ2, CQ4</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A17:D17 | A=Organization | B=Class | C=Organisation Custom Post Type with name, contact details and links to its services or care centres. | D=CQ3, CQ8</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A18:D18 | A=SupportService | B=Class | C=Support Service Custom Post Type with phone, location, supported condition and organisation fields. | D=CQ3</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A19:D19 | A=CareCentre | B=Class | C=Care Centre Custom Post Type with contact, location, staff and language information. | D=CQ8</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A20:D20 | A=Location | B=Class | C=Hierarchical location taxonomy plus postcode field, used to filter services and care centres by state or area. | D=CQ3, CQ8</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A21:D21 | A=Language | B=Class | C=Language taxonomy assigned to Guides and staff records, with a Chinese-language filter. | D=CQ7, CQ8</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A22:D22 | A=DocumentFormat | B=Class | C=Guide format taxonomy/custom field (for example, PDF or HTML), with download and print links. | D=CQ4</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A23:D23 | A=PrivacyPolicy | B=Class | C=Static WordPress Privacy Policy page linked in the footer and from search or feedback notices. | D=CQ5</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A24:D24 | A=caresFor (Carer → OlderAdult) | B=Relationship | C=No stored WordPress relationship because the site does not keep personal care profiles. Represent it only through example scenarios in carer guidance. | D=CQ1, CQ2, CQ3</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A25:D25 | A=hasCondition (OlderAdult → HealthCondition) | B=Relationship | C=No stored personal-health relationship. Users browse or filter by condition without saving a personal profile. | D=CQ1, CQ2, CQ3, CQ6</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A26:D26 | A=addresses (Guide → HealthCondition) | B=Relationship | C=Condition taxonomy/reference field on each Guide; condition pages automatically list related Guides. | D=CQ1, CQ2, CQ6, CQ7</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A27:D27 | A=isRelatedTo (Guide → InformationTopic) | B=Relationship | C=Topic taxonomy/reference field linking each Guide to relevant information topics so users can find Guides based on their needs | D=CQ1, CQ2, CQ6, CQ7</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A28:D28 | A=isReviewedBy (Guide → HealthcareProfessional) | B=Relationship | C=Reviewer post/reference field on each Guide, displayed with credentials and the last-reviewed date. | D=CQ2</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A29:D29 | A=isLocatedIn (OlderAdult OR SupportService OR CareCentre → Location) | B=Relationship | C=Location field/taxonomy assigned to Older Adults, Support Services and Care Centres, enabling support options to be matched or filtered by the same area. | D=CQ3, CQ8</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A30:D30 | A=isIntendedFor (Guide → Person) | B=Relationship | C=Audience taxonomy assigned to Guides using specific audience terms such as Carer and OlderAdult, with corresponding audience filters | D=CQ4, CQ7</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A31:D31 | A=isAvailableInFormat (Guide → DocumentFormat) | B=Relationship | C=Document-format taxonomy/custom field plus downloadable or printable file links on the Guide page. | D=CQ4</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A32:D32 | A=hasSymptom (HealthCondition → Symptom) | B=Relationship | C=Post-reference field linking each Health Condition to relevant Symptom records; shown as a related-symptoms list. | D=CQ5, CQ6</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A33:D33 | A=describes (Guide → Symptom) | B=Relationship | C=Symptom reference/taxonomy field on each Guide; Symptom pages list Guides that describe them. | D=CQ5, CQ6</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A34:D34 | A=isGovernedBy (Guide → PrivacyPolicy) | B=Relationship | C=Implemented site-wide through the Privacy Policy link and public search that requires no login or personal data; no separate relationship record. | D=CQ5</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A35:D35 | A=isAvailableIn (Guide → Language (Chinese)) | B=Relationship | C=Language taxonomy on each Guide, with a Chinese filter and links to translated versions. | D=CQ7</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A36:D36 | A=hasStaffMember (CareCentre → StaffMember) | B=Relationship | C=Staff repeater/reference field on each CareCentre page, showing staff names and roles relevant to service enquiries. | D=CQ8</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A37:D37 | A=speaksLanguage (StaffMember → Language (Chinese)) | B=Relationship | C=Language field/taxonomy on each staff entry; supports filtering CareCentres for Chinese-speaking staff. | D=CQ8</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A5:D5 | A=Person | B=Class | C=No standalone public profile. Represented only through author, reviewer or staff display fields on relevant content; personal accounts are outside the initial scope. | D=CQ1, CQ2, CQ3, CQ4, CQ5, CQ6, CQ7, CQ8</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A6:D6 | A=Carer | B=Class | C=Audience taxonomy and a &apos;For Carers&apos; landing page; no proxy account or access to an older person&apos;s health information. | D=CQ1, CQ2, CQ3, CQ4</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A7:D7 | A=OlderAdult | B=Class | C=Audience taxonomy and a &apos;For Older People&apos; landing page; no personal health profile is stored. | D=CQ1, CQ2, CQ3, CQ5, CQ6, CQ7, CQ8</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A8:D8 | A=HealthcareProfessional | B=Class | C=Reviewer record/reference field storing name, professional role and credentials; displayed with each reviewed Guide. | D=CQ2</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <worksheet:traceabilityRow>6. Traceability!A9:D9 | A=StaffMember | B=Class | C=Staff name, role and language fields attached to a CareCentre record; not a WordPress user account. | D=CQ8</worksheet:traceabilityRow>
        <rdfs:comment>Built by exact transcription of DigitalCare_Model_Worksheet.xlsx. The worksheet Ontology IRI cell is blank; this provisional IRI is derived only from the immutable worksheet SHA-256.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Digital Care — The Star</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


